Appendix A-യിലെ timeline positions-നെ ഏഴ്-slot rolling ring-ൽ സൂക്ഷിക്കാൻ വേണ്ട index mapping clean Stage 1 control. slot(p)=1+regularMod(p,7). negative hidden positions-നായി source നേരിട്ട് negative remainder ആശ്രയിക്കാതെ തുല്യ positive representatives ഉപയോഗിക്കുന്നു. i=1-ൽ current,prev1,prev3,prev7 = 2,1,6,2; i=46-ൽ = 5,4,2,5; current slot prev7 slot-നോട് 46 തവണയും തുല്യമാണ്, commit പഴയ prev7 വായിച്ചതിന് ശേഷമേ നടക്കാവൂ.

Hamlet, visible drop index i സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Juliet, current slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, prev1 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, prev3 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Macbeth, prev7 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Lady Macbeth, current-prev7 equality count സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ophelia, first current slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Cordelia, first prev1 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Desdemona, first prev3 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Portia, first prev7 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Viola, last current slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Miranda, last prev1 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ariel, last prev3 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Caliban, last prev7 slot സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, assignment, branch, output സഹായിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: counters.

Scene I: i=1, equality count=0.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero: You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are nothing.
[Exeunt]

Act II: slot mapping for i=1..46.

Scene I: current slot = 1 + i mod 7.
[Enter Prospero and Juliet]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between Hamlet and the sum of the sum of a big big hero and a big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: prev1 slot = 1 + (i-1) mod 7.
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between Hamlet and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and the sum of the sum of a big big hero and a big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene III: prev3 slot = 1 + regularMod(i-3,7) = 1 + (i+4) mod 7 for i>=1.
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of Hamlet and a big big hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and the sum of the sum of a big big hero and a big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene IV: prev7 slot = 1 + regularMod(i-7,7) = current slot.
[Enter Prospero and Macbeth]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between Hamlet and the sum of the sum of a big big hero and a big hero and a hero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene V: current == prev7 count.
[Enter Juliet and Prospero]
Juliet: Am I as good as Macbeth?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene VI. Let us proceed to scene VII.
[Exeunt]

Scene VI: equality count increment.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero. Let us proceed to scene VII.
[Exeunt]

Scene VII: i=1 mapping capture.
[Enter Hamlet and Prospero]
Hamlet: Am I as good as a hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene VIII. Let us proceed to scene XII.
[Exeunt]

Scene VIII: first current.
[Enter Juliet and Ophelia]
Juliet: You are as good as Juliet.
[Exeunt]

Scene IX: first prev1.
[Enter Romeo and Cordelia]
Romeo: You are as good as Romeo.
[Exeunt]

Scene X: first prev3.
[Enter Othello and Desdemona]
Othello: You are as good as Othello.
[Exeunt]

Scene XI: first prev7.
[Enter Macbeth and Portia]
Macbeth: You are as good as Macbeth.
[Exeunt]

Scene XII: i=46 mapping capture or loop.
[Enter Hamlet and Prospero]
Hamlet: Am I as good as the sum of the sum of a big big big big big hero and a big big big hero and the sum of a big big hero and a big hero?
Prospero: If so, let us proceed to scene XIII. Let us proceed to scene XVII.
[Exeunt]

Scene XIII: last current.
[Enter Juliet and Viola]
Juliet: You are as good as Juliet.
[Exeunt]

Scene XIV: last prev1.
[Enter Romeo and Miranda]
Romeo: You are as good as Romeo.
[Exeunt]

Scene XV: last prev3.
[Enter Othello and Ariel]
Othello: You are as good as Othello.
[Exeunt]

Scene XVI: last prev7.
[Enter Macbeth and Caliban]
Macbeth: You are as good as Macbeth. Let us proceed to act III.
[Exeunt]

Scene XVII: i increment.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero. Let us return to scene I.
[Exeunt]

Act III: expected mapping outputs.

Scene I: i=1 -> 2,1,6,2.
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Cordelia]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Desdemona]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Portia]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: i=46 -> 5,4,2,5.
[Enter Prospero and Viola]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Miranda]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ariel]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Caliban]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

Scene III: current-prev7 equality count = 46.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
